xnu 0373: list a directory with the plain readdir the driver actually fills

`VNODE_READDIR_EXTENDED` answers an empty buffer with no error, even for a
directory that has entries: measured 2026-11-19, `/private/var/vm` listed its
twenty entries on a kernel that asked for plain `struct dirent` and listed nothing
on one that asked for `struct direntry`. The plain call has its own quirk -- it
writes the two dot entries as `struct hfs_stddotentry`, 12 bytes each, and only
then packs `struct dirent` -- so the walk starts 24 bytes in and treats a record
that does not fit as the end of the batch.

This matters because the volume loses tens of megabytes a minute to something the
port cannot name: `/private/var/log` and `/private/var/db/diagnostics` answer
`deltree -> 0 files` while their catalog valence is 5 and 10, so the files eating
the disk are invisible until the listing works.

